From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:14:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] 9703: x86: Read CS in real mode instead of computing it

x86: Read CS in real mode instead of computing it

In real mode, currentCS wrote CS = (inst_next >> 4) & 0xf000 before
exporting it. That is only the real code segment when CS is a multiple
of 0x1000, so CS: operands and near indirect CALL and JMP resolved into
the wrong segment and overwrote CS for the rest of the function.

currentCS now exports CS. The MZ loader already sets CS for each block.
Where nothing sets it, x86-16-real.pspec supplies the value currentCS
used to compute, one tracked_set per 64K, so COM files, ROMs and raw
binaries resolve as before.

Direct CALLF writes the callee's segment into CS, and static analysis
continues in the caller after the call, so the caller's CS is restored
after the call op, as the indirect forms need too.

Constant propagation treats a zero read from a register as a suspect
constant, which dropped references through segment 0 once CS came from
context. In real-mode segmented spaces a zero segment base now counts
as segment 0. Protected mode keeps the old handling, since selector 0
is the null selector there.

x86: Handle overlays in the real-mode segment check, trim comments

The real-mode check in SymbolicPropogator now uses the physical space of
the instruction address, so code in an overlay of the real-mode ram
space treats a zero segment as segment 0 like the base space does.

The "segment_pcode" payload name is now a constant instead of three
string literals.

Removed comments that restated the code and shortened the rest.
